gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg","html_url":"https://github.com/kisg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kisg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T00:09:22Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T00:09:22Z","body":"@Ivorforce @lawnjelly This PR handles GLOBAL_GET_CACHED reinitialization support.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5901448131/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5902966143","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123552#issuecomment-5902966143","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123552","id":5902966143,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABX9gdfw","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-30T02:37:01Z","updated_at":"2026-09-30T03:22:14Z","body":"I'm wondering whether instead we can simply bump the version number in the ProjectSettings when restarting, and everything should just work :tm: .\r\n\r\nAll the cached variables will be seen as out of date.\r\nThis isn't intended to be used with complex variables (only things like e.g. bool and int) so the only question is whether you can transfer the old (version + 1) to the new `ProjectSettings` on restart.\r\n\r\nThere's also wraparound, but you could calculate the odds of this occurring, or even just use 64 bit version.\r\n\r\n## Ordering\r\nNow if `GLOBAL_GET_CACHED` is called _before_ the new `ProjectSettings` is setup, it's a problem. But this should not be happening already (it would be a bug), and we could probably `DEV_ASSERT()` this.\r\n\r\nAgain this ties in with **singletons are evil**. If you want to be able to re-run, imo they should be replaced by globals with strict explicit construction / destruction ordering.\r\n\r\nEssentially, if the boot order is wrong, if we can, we should probably fix the order to protect against it, rather than adding a registry to clean up after it.\r\n\r\n## Putting the data in a struct\r\nThis is actually an improvement purely from a namespace point of view, the existing method is probably more historical from development of the macro, maybe it didn't occur to me to put it in a struct at the time. Might be worth a separate PR (UPDATE - looking at this, there are some gotchas, so it may or may not be worth doing).","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5902966143/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5932102492","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123552#issuecomment-5932102492","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123552","id":5932102492,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYZSzXA","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T13:07:39Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T13:07:39Z","body":"Actually thinking about it, I'm not sure there's a pressing case to change it to 64 bit.\r\n\r\nThe counter only increments when project settings are _written_ (rather than read), so there would need to be 4 billion project settings changes for an overflow, which seems a tad unlikely, unless something was misusing project settings _really_ badly (which would be a bug itself).\r\n\r\nIt would probably be fine for a thousand years or so of uptime.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5932102492/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5932139149","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123552#issuecomment-5932139149","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123552","id":5932139149,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYZVCjQ","user":{"login":"konczg","id":38984895,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM4OTg0ODk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/38984895?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg","html_url":"https://github.com/konczg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konczg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T13:09:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T13:09:51Z","body":"@lawnjelly You are right, I implemented a process-monotonic 64-bit version counter, so that cached global settings can get refreshed after reinit without the unnecessary additional runtime machinery","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5932139149/reactions","total